.TH OSI-WATCH 1 2026-11-13 "osi 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
osi-watch \- Attaches to a Circuitry orchestration run already in progress, or
watches its finished state.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBosi watch\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-\-plan\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR]
[\fB\-e \fR] [\fB\-\-log\fR] [\fB\-\-glance\fR] [\fB\-\-once\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-animation\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-history\fR]
<\fITARGET\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Attaches to a Circuitry orchestration run already in progress, or watches its
finished state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-plan\fR \fI<doc.yml>\fR
Compiles this document into a plan, the same one a live \fBosi <doc>\fR run of
it would have from the start \-\- without it, container detection (an
\fBif\fR/loop vs. a leaf) can briefly fall back to a snapshot it hasn\*(Aqt
seen yet instead
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<config.json>\fR
The config \fB\-\-plan\fR\*(Aqs document should be checked against \-\- the
same \fBconfig.json\fR the watched run itself used, if any. Needed for a
document whose plan depends on a config\-defined
\fBconcurrency_groups\fR/\fBruntime:\fR block; without it, \fB\-\-plan\fR
still compiles, just without that merge
.TP
\fB\-e\fR \fI<key=value>\fR
\fB\-e key=value\fR inputs \fB\-\-plan\fR\*(Aqs document needs to compile \-\-
the same ones the watched run itself was given, if any
.TP
\fB\-\-log\fR
Forces the plain\-text stream even on a TTY \-\- the TUI\*(Aqs default
otherwise, the same split \fBosi <doc>\fR makes
.TP
\fB\-\-glance\fR
Shows only the header line, without the tabs, rewritten in place about once a
second \-\- for a tmux status line. Can\*(Aqt be combined with \fB\-\-log\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-once\fR
With \fB\-\-glance\fR: prints the current line once and exits 0, rather than
watching \-\- for a tmux status line that runs its own command on a timer
instead of leaving one process attached
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-animation\fR
Switches off the scope icon\*(Aqs trace: the header draws a still frame in its
place instead
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fI<THEME>\fR
The colour theme. \fBOSI_THEME\fR is used when this isn\*(Aqt given;
\fBterminal\fR (today\*(Aqs look) otherwise

\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
terminal
.IP \(bu 2
dracula
.IP \(bu 2
nord
.IP \(bu 2
solarized\-dark
.IP \(bu 2
solarized\-light
.IP \(bu 2
gruvbox\-dark
.IP \(bu 2
gruvbox\-light
.IP \(bu 2
catppuccin\-mocha
.IP \(bu 2
catppuccin\-latte
.IP \(bu 2
tokyo\-night
.IP \(bu 2
one\-dark
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-history\fR
Turns run history off \-\- see \fBosi \-\-help\fR\*(Aqs \fB\-\-no\-history\fR
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
A run directory, or a \fBstate.live.json\fR file directly
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B osi watch ./run
Attaches to the run directory a prior osi orchestration.yml --out-dir ./run
launch wrote.
.TP
.B osi watch ./run/state.live.json --plan orchestration.yml
Watches a live state file directly, compiling orchestration.yml into the same
plan the live run started from.
.TP
.B osi watch ./run --glance --once
Prints the current header line for a tmux status line and exits, instead of
watching.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OSI_THEME
The colour theme, when --theme isn't given. terminal (today's look) otherwise.
.TP
.B OSI_HISTORY
OSI_HISTORY=off turns run history off, the same as --no-history: nothing is
read or written, and no history directory is created.
.TP
.B OSI_HISTORY_DIR
Overrides osi's history directory (see FILES below).
.TP
.B OSI_RUNS_DIR
Overrides osi's run registry directory (see FILES below).
.TP
.B OSI_PROCESS_SCAN
OSI_PROCESS_SCAN=0 limits bare osi's discovery (no orchestration, no TTY, or
--log) to the run registry, skipping the process scan and any state.live.json
in the current directory.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
The base osi's history and run registry directories are rooted under, when
OSI_HISTORY_DIR/OSI_RUNS_DIR aren't set.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Preferred over XDG_STATE_HOME for the run registry alone (a live run's pid
file), when it's set.
.TP
.B CI
Forces the plain-text stream, the same as --log.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/circuitry/osi/history/
Per-document run history: one record per finished run, read back for the
Recent Runs table and ETA estimates. OSI_HISTORY_DIR overrides this directory;
OSI_HISTORY=off or --no-history disables it entirely.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/circuitry/osi/runs/
The run registry: one file per run osi launched or is watching, used by bare
osi's discovery and pruned once a run's pid is no longer alive. OSI_RUNS_DIR
overrides this directory; $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/circuitry/osi/runs is tried first
when set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The watched or launched run finished without error.
.TP
.B 1 and other
osi exits with the engine's own exit code, passed through unchanged -- a child
process's own code if it had one, or 128 plus the signal number that killed
it. 1 covers an ordinary failure, or osi being unable to start or attach to
the run at all.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option, a missing required argument, or an
unknown osi man page. Never from the watched or launched engine itself.
.TP
.B 129
The run ended on SIGHUP (128 + 1).
.TP
.B 130
The run ended on SIGINT, Ctrl-C (128 + 2).
.TP
.B 143
The run ended on SIGTERM (128 + 15).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR osi (1),
.BR osi\-watch (1),
.BR cof (1),
.BR cof\-run (1),
.BR electricity (1)
